questions.description:
Assume a development build, no Fast Refresh, and `<StrictMode>` at the root.

```tsx
function Probe() {
  console.log('render');
  useEffect(() => {
    console.log('setup');
    return () => console.log('cleanup');
  }, []);
  return null;
}
```

Assume development Strict Mode and an initial `count` of `0`.

```tsx
<button onClick={() => {
  setCount(c => {
    console.log('updater', c);
    return c + 1;
  });
}}>Increment</button>
```

The lint warning is suppressed. Initially, `count` is `0` and `increment` is `1`. After the interval starts, the user changes `increment` to `5`.

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  const id = setInterval(() => {
    setCount(count + increment);
  }, 1000);
  return () => clearInterval(id);
}, []);
```

Assume a production build. The component was committed with `roomId = 'general'`, then re-renders and commits with `roomId = 'travel'`.

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  connect(roomId);
  return () => disconnect(roomId);
}, [roomId]);
```

Assume `firstName = 'Ada'`, `lastName = 'Lovelace'`, and no other updates.

```tsx
const [fullName, setFullName] = useState('');
useEffect(() => {
  setFullName(firstName + ' ' + lastName);
}, [firstName, lastName]);
return <p>{fullName}</p>;
```

The current render has `number = 0`.

```tsx
function handleClick() {
  setNumber(number + 5);
  setTimeout(() => console.log(number), 1000);
}
```

```tsx
setNumber(number + 1);
setNumber(number + 1);
setNumber(number + 1);
```

```tsx
setNumber(number + 5);
setNumber(n => n + 1);
setNumber(42);
```

Assume React Compiler is off. `Child` is an ordinary function component, not wrapped in `memo`. The parent increments `parentCount`, while `label` stays `'Save'`.

```tsx
function Parent() {
  const [parentCount, setParentCount] = useState(0);
  return <Child label="Save" />;
}
```

Assume React Compiler is off.

```tsx
const Chart = memo(function Chart({ options }) {
  // expensive render
});

function Dashboard({ theme }) {
  const [tick, setTick] = useState(0);
  return <Chart options={{ theme }} />;
}
```

Assume `todos` is a prop owned by the parent.

```tsx
const visible = useMemo(() => {
  todos.push({ id: 'temp', text: 'Inspect' });
  return todos.filter(todo => !todo.done);
}, [todos]);
```

```tsx
function Counter() {
  const countRef = useRef(0);
  return (
    <button onClick={() => countRef.current++}>
      {countRef.current}
    </button>
  );
}
```

```tsx
function Albums() {
  const response = use(fetch('/api/albums'));
  // ...
}
```

```tsx
function Results() {
  const [data, setData] = useState(null);
  useEffect(() => {
    fetch('/api/results').then(r => r.json()).then(setData);
  }, []);
  return data ? <List data={data} /> : null;
}
```

`Results` is inside `<Suspense fallback={<Spinner />}>`.
